From 2e0d6ecea2e79d7a491204b9b34d5c37a2b1d08c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felicitas Pojtinger <felicitas@pojtinger.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:44:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] docs: Add more precise descriptions to root MCP agent instructions

Signed-off-by: Felicitas Pojtinger <felicitas@pojtinger.com>
---
diff --git a/main.go b/main.go
index eed23558f307db3ccc0df1359abdcbaec2a4b98a..44e4f8f8cfcc4919fa289cefabb243cde2a640e2 100644
--- a/main.go
+++ b/main.go
@@ -56,15 +56,27 @@ 		&mcp.ServerOptions{
 			Logger: logger,
 			Instructions: `Never call flash.multiFlash or flash.flashFile on a BROM device. It answers OKAY and writes nothing.
 
-Read flash.getDevices first. Manufacturer DFU with productId 1001 means BROM. Manufacturer U-Boot means U-Boot fastboot.
+Read flash.getDevices first. Manufacturer DFU means BROM. Manufacturer U-Boot means U-Boot fastboot. productId 1001 appears in both modes.
 
-Upload every image before a stage or flash. files.getFiles names the uploads.
+To enter BROM, run target.reset, then target.enterFDL. The relay state does not prove the mode. Confirm the mode with flash.getDevices.
+
+Upload the images of the build that you want to flash. files.getFiles also lists uploads from earlier builds, so replace them. Each entry needs the uploadCommand.
 
-BROM: stage FSBL.bin, continue. Read flash.getDevices. Stage u-boot.itb, continue.
+BROM: stage FSBL.bin, then continue. Read flash.getDevices. Run flash.oem with speed:super-speed only when superSpeedCapable is true. Stage u-boot.itb, then continue. Read flash.getDevices.
 
-U-Boot: read mtd-size and blk-size. Call flash.multiFlash with partition_<mtd-size>.json and partition_<blk-size>.json.
+Read flash.getDevices after each flash.oem call.
 
-Every partition in a table needs offset and size. The device builds its GPT from them.`,
+U-Boot: read mtd-size and blk-size. Build the table inline from partition_<mtd-size>.json and partition_<blk-size>.json. Use the mtd table only when that file exists, otherwise flash the gpt table only. A disk image such as sdcard.img is not a table.
+
+Every partition needs name, offset, size and image. The device builds its GPT from offset and size. Call flash.multiFlash with reboot true when the flash must boot the new system.
+
+Watch a running flash with flash.getJobs. Read status, partition, sentBytes, totalBytes and error.
+
+Start serial buffering before a reset. serial.getConsoles lists the console paths. serial.readFrom returns the captured output. A boot succeeded when the log reaches K3-Buildroot login:.
+
+The KVM path shows the screen. kvm.getVideoCaptureDevices lists the capture path, and kvm.takeScreenshot returns a JPEG. kvm.getInputDevices lists the input path for kvm.sendMouseInput and kvm.pressKeys. A panel launcher needs a doubleClick.
+
+No fastboot device means no gadget. Run target.reset, then target.enterFDL, then read flash.getDevices again. The relays press the RST and FDL buttons only.`,
 		},
 	)
 	handler.AddReceivingMiddleware(svc.LogIncoming(logger))

